{"step_index":674,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T17:27:46Z","thinking":"The plan is to enhance the application's user interface with a futuristic aesthetic. This involves incorporating specific Google Fonts (Orbitron, Rajdhani, and JetBrains Mono) to establish a distinctive visual identity. The intention is also to set a dark, impactful background color.\n\n\nFocus shifted to detailed styling, including gradient backgrounds, font applications (Orbitron for headings, Rajdhani elsewhere), and a specific dark color scheme. Observed the need for custom CSS rules to address the card containers and apply effects like blur, shadow, and border modifications to simulate a futuristic aesthetic. This approach aims to create visual consistency across UI elements.\n\n\nFurther investigation into detailed visual elements reveals specific CSS configurations for HUD banners and pulse dot animations. The goal is to apply futuristic styling to these elements. Observed configurations for border effects, box shadows, background gradients, and keyframe animations will now be applied.\n\n\nFocused now on styling the status badges, planning to apply specific color palettes to indicate status (e.g., success, warning). Considering the appropriate CSS for rounded corners, font properties, and subtle shadow effects to provide visual cues.\n\nNeed to create CSS classes to ensure these styles can be reused across the application and maintain a consistent look. The specific color assignments will correlate to the status indicators, offering visual feedback to the user.\n\n\nRefining the color palettes for UI elements, specifically the \"evidence-box,\" \"metric-pane,\" and tab styles. Focused on adjusting the CSS to ensure proper background, border, and shadow effects for each component. The aim is to create visual distinctions based on the status indicators (HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW) and overall visual style.\n\n\nNow examining the detailed CSS for the tab navigation and metric display components. The focus is to apply the specified fonts (Rajdhani, JetBrains Mono) and color schemes to these elements to ensure consistent styling. Considering the application of subtle hover effects and selected state highlighting for the tab navigation.\n\nNext, the style rules for buttons are under review, planning the application of Rajdhani font, text transformations, and border radius to harmonize the button styles with the overall futuristic aesthetic.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\"\"\nVisual Inspection & Defect Root-Cause Assistant\nStreamlit main application with futuristic industrial command-center aesthetic\n\"\"\"\nimport io\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pandas as pd\nimport streamlit as st\nfrom PIL import Image\n\n# ── Path setup ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nROOT = Path(__file__).parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n\nfrom modules.defect_detector  import load_model, run_inference\nfrom modules.defect_registry  import DefectRegistry\nfrom modules.production_analyzer import load_dataset, load_csv, analyze, compare_models, estimate_wip\nfrom modules.root_cause       import correlate, drift_analysis, flag_novel\nfrom modules.profitability    import compute_financials, what_if, impact_delta\nfrom utils.chart_helpers      import (\n    defect_donut, defect_type_bar, confidence_histogram, defect_trend,\n    utilization_bar, waiting_time_bar, multi_model_radar,\n    financial_waterfall, margin_comparison_bar,\n)\nfrom utils.constants import DEFECT_CLASSES, STATUS_COLORS\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Page Config\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nst.set_page_config(\n    page_title=\"Industrial AI Platform\",\n    layout=\"wide\",\n    initial_sidebar_state=\"expanded\",\n)\n\n# ── Futuristic Cyber Industrial UI Styling ────────────────────────────────────\nst.markdown(\"\"\"\n<style>\n    @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Orbitron:wght@500;700;900&family=Rajdhani:wght@500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;700&display=swap');\n\n    /* Global Cyber Canvas */\n    .stApp {\n        background-color: #050711;\n        background-image: \n            radial-gradient(at 0% 0%, rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.08) 0px, transparent 50%),\n            radial-gradient(at 100% 0%, rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.08) 0px, transparent 50%),\n            radial-gradient(at 50% 100%, rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.05) 0px, transparent 50%);\n        font-family: 'Rajdhani', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif;\n        letter-spacing: 0.2px;\n    }\n    \n    /* Headers with Futuristic Font */\n    h1, h2, h3 {\n        font-family: 'Orbitron', -apple-system, sans-serif !important;\n        font-weight: 700 !important;\n        letter-spacing: 0.8px !important;\n        color: #f8fafc !important;\n        text-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.15);\n    }\n    h4, h5, h6 {\n        font-family: 'Rajdhani', sans-serif !important;\n        font-weight: 700 !important;\n        letter-spacing: 0.5px !important;\n        color: #e2e8f0 !important;\n    }\n\n    /* Futuristic Card Containers */\n    [data-testid=\"stVerticalBlockBorderWrapper\"] {\n        background: rgba(11, 17, 33, 0.75) !important;\n        border: 1px solid rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.16) !important;\n        border-radius: 12px !important;\n        backdrop-filter: blur(16px) !important;\n        -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px) !important;\n        box-shadow: 0 8px 32px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45), inset 0 1px 0 0 rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.15) !important;\n        transition: border-color 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease;\n    }\n    [data-testid=\"stVerticalBlockBorderWrapper\"]:hover {\n        border-color: rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.32) !important;\n        box-shadow: 0 10px 40px 0 rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.1), inset 0 1px 0 0 rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.25) !important;\n    }\n\n    /* Live Telemetry Pulse Dot */\n    .pulse-dot {\n        display: inline-block;\n        width: 8px;\n        height: 8px;\n        border-radius: 50%;\n        background-color: #00f0ff;\n        box-shadow: 0 0 10px #00f0ff;\n        animation: pulse_glow 2s infinite ease-in-out;\n        margin-right: 6px;\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n    .pulse-dot.green {\n        background-color: #10b981;\n        box-shadow: 0 0 10px #10b981;\n    }\n    @keyframes pulse_glow {\n        0% { transform: scale(0.95); opacity: 0.8; box-shadow: 0 0 4px currentColor; }\n        50% { transform: scale(1.25); opacity: 1; box-shadow: 0 0 14px currentColor; }\n        100% { transform: scale(0.95); opacity: 0.8; box-shadow: 0 0 4px currentColor; }\n    }\n\n    /* Futuristic HUD Telemetry Banner */\n    .hud-banner {\n        display: flex;\n        align-items: center;\n        justify-content: space-between;\n        background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.08) 0%, rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.04) 100%);\n        border: 1px solid rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.25);\n        border-radius: 10px;\n        padding: 10px 18px;\n        margin-bottom: 12px;\n        font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;\n        font-size: 11px;\n        color: #94a3b8;\n        letter-spacing: 0.8px;\n    }\n    .hud-banner .status-val {\n        color: #00f0ff;\n        font-weight: 700;\n    }\n\n    /* Badges */\n    .badge {\n        display: inline-block;\n        padding: 4px 12px;\n        border-radius: 4px;\n        font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;\n        font-size: 11px;\n        font-weight: 700;\n        letter-spacing: 0.8px;\n        text-transform: uppercase;\n        border: 1px solid transparent;\n    }\n    .badge-DEFECT    { background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.15); color: #ff3366; border-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.4); box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.2); }\n    .badge-PASS      { background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.15); color: #05df9d; border-color: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.4); box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.2); }\n    .badge-UNCERTAIN { background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.15); color: #ffaa00; border-color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.4); box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.2); }\n    .badge-NOVEL     { background: rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.15); color: #c084fc; border-color: rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.4); box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.2); }\n    .badge-CRITICAL  { background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.15); color: #ff3366; border-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.4); box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.2); }\n    .badge-WARNING   { background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.15); color: #ffaa00; border-color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.4); box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.2); }\n    .badge-OPTIMAL   { background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.15); color: #05df9d; border-color: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.4); box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.2); }\n    .badge-HIGH      { background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.15); color: #ff3366; border-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.4); }\n    .badge-MEDIUM    { background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.15); color: #ffaa00; border-color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.4); }\n    .badge-LOW       { background: rgba(100, 116, 139, 0.15); color: #94a3b8; border-color: rgba(100, 116, 139, 0.4); }\n\n    /* Evidence Box */\n    .evidence-box {\n        background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85);\n        border: 1px solid rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.18);\n        border-radius: 8px;\n        padding: 16px 18px;\n        margin-bottom: 12px;\n        border-left: 4px solid #00f0ff;\n        box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);\n    }\n    .evidence-box.HIGH     { border-left-color: #ff3366; }\n    .evidence-box.CRITICAL { border-left-color: #ff3366; }\n    .evidence-box.MEDIUM   { border-left-color: #ffaa00; }\n    .evidence-box.WARNING  { border-left-color: #ffaa00; }\n    .evidence-box.LOW      { border-left-color: #64748b; }\n    .evidence-box.OPTIMAL  { border-left-color: #05df9d; }\n\n    /* Metric Pane */\n    .metric-pane {\n        background: rgba(13, 20, 38, 0.7);\n        border: 1px solid rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.15);\n        border-radius: 8px;\n        padding: 14px 16px;\n        margin-bottom: 10px;\n        box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);\n    }\n\n    /* Tabs Styling */\n    .stTabs [data-baseweb=\"tab-list\"] {\n        gap: 10px;\n        margin-bottom: 18px;\n        background: rgba(11, 17, 33, 0.6);\n        padding: 6px;\n        border-radius: 12px;\n        border: 1px solid rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.12);\n    }\n    .stTabs [data-baseweb=\"tab\"] {\n        font-family: 'Rajdhani', sans-serif;\n        font-size: 15px;\n        font-weight: 700;\n        letter-spacing: 0.6px;\n        padding: 10px 22px;\n        background-color: transparent;\n        border: 1px solid transparent;\n        border-radius: 8px;\n        color: #94a3b8;\n        transition: all 0.25s ease;\n    }\n    .stTabs [data-baseweb=\"tab\"]:hover {\n        color: #00f0ff;\n        background-color: rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.06);\n    }\n    .stTabs [aria-selected=\"true\"] {\n        background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.15) 0%, rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.15) 100%) !important;\n        color: #00f0ff !important;\n        border-color: rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.4) !important;\n        box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.15);\n    }\n\n    /* Streamlit Metrics */\n    [data-testid=\"stMetricValue\"] {\n        font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace !important;\n        font-weight: 700 !important;\n        color: #f8fafc !important;\n    }\n    [data-testid=\"stMetricLabel\"] {\n        font-family: 'Rajdhani', sans-serif !important;\n        font-size: 13px !important;\n        font-weight: 600 !important;\n        letter-spacing: 0.6px !important;\n        text-transform: uppercase !important;\n        color: #94a3b8 !important;\n    }\n\n    /* Cyber Buttons */\n    .stButton>button {\n        font-family: 'Rajdhani', sans-serif !important;\n        font-weight: 700 !important;\n        letter-spacing: 0.8px !important;\n        text-transform: uppercase !important;\n        border-radius: 8px !important;\n        border: 1px solid rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.3) !important;\n        background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f172a 0%, #1e293b 100%) !important;\n        color: #f8fafc !important;\n        transition: all 0.25s ease !important;\n    }\n    .stButton>button:hover {\n        border-color: #00f0ff !important;\n        box-shadow: 0 0 18px rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.35) !important;\n        transform: translateY(-1px);\n    }\n    .stButton>button[kind=\"primary\"] {\n        background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0077b6 0%, #00b4d8 100%) !important;\n        border-color: #00f0ff !important;\n        color: #ffffff !important;\n        box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.25) !important;\n    }\n    .stButton>button[kind=\"primary\"]:hover {\n        box-shadow: 0 0 25px rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.55) !important;\n    }\n</style>\n\"\"\", unsafe_allow_html=True)\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Session State Initialisation\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nif 'registry' not in st.session_state:\n    st.session_state.registry = DefectRegistry()\nif 'annotated_images' not in st.session_state:\n    st.session_state.annotated_images = {}\nif 'model_data' not in st.session_state:\n    st.session_state.model_data = {}\nif 'analyses' not in st.session_state:\n    st.session_state.analyses = {}\nif 'yolo_model' not in st.session_state:\n    st.session_state.yolo_model = None\nif 'model_load_error' not in st.session_state:\n    st.session_state.model_load_error = None\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Sidebar\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nwith st.sidebar:\n    st.markdown(\"### SYSTEM CONTROL\")\n    st.caption(\"AI Neural Engine, Telemetry Ingestion & Economic Parameters\")\n    st.divider()\n\n    # AI Model Engine\n    with st.container(border=True):\n        st.markdown(\"**NEURAL INFERENCE ENGINE**\")\n        custom_pt = st.text_input(\n            \"Weights File (.pt)\",\n            placeholder=r\"D:\\acceleration\\best.pt\",\n            label_visibility=\"collapsed\",\n        )\n        if st.button(\"Initialize Neural Core\", use_container_width=True):\n            with st.spinner(\"Compiling YOLOv8 neural pipeline...\"):\n                mdl, err = load_model(custom_pt or None)\n                st.session_state.yolo_model = mdl\n                st.session_state.model_load_error = err\n            if mdl:\n                st.success(\"Neural Core Active.\")\n            else:\n                st.error(f\"Error: {err}\")\n\n        # Auto-load on initial run\n        if st.session_state.yolo_model is None and st.session_state.model_load_error is None:\n            mdl, err = load_model(custom_pt or None)\n            st.session_state.yolo_model = mdl\n            st.session_state.model_load_error = err\n\n        if st.session_state.yolo_model:\n            st.markdown(\"<small><span class='pulse-dot green'></span> <b>STATUS:</b> ACTIVE (YOLOv8 Core)</small>\", unsafe_allow_html=True)\n        elif st.session_state.model_load_error:\n            st.caption(f\"Status: {st.session_state.model_load_error[:55]}...\")\n\n    # Inspection Boundary\n    with st.container(border=True):\n        st.markdown(\"**DECISION BOUNDARY**\")\n        conf_threshold = st.slider(\n            \"Confidence Cutoff\",\n            min_value=0.20, max_value=0.90, value=0.45, step=0.05,\n            help=\"Confidence >= Cutoff: Classified. Below Cutoff: UNCERTAIN. < 0.25: NOVEL.\",\n        )\n\n    # Production Datasets (.CSV, .XLSX, .XLS)\n    with st.container(border=True):\n        st.markdown(\"**TELEMETRY DATASETS**\")\n        st.caption(\"Upload .csv, .xlsx, or .xls Arena simulations\")\n\n        def _upload_dataset(label, model_key, uploader_key):\n            f = st.file_uploader(label, type=['csv', 'xlsx', 'xls'], key=uploader_key)\n            if f:\n                df, err = load_dataset(f)\n                if err:\n                    st.error(f\"Error reading {f.name}: {err}\")\n                else:\n                    st.session_state.model_data[model_key] = df\n                    analysis = analyze(df)\n                    if analysis:\n                        st.session_state.analyses[model_key] = analysis\n                        st.success(f\"Loaded {model_key} ({len(df)} rows)\")\n                    else:\n                        st.warning(f\"Loaded {model_key}, but no station telemetry recognized.\")\n\n        _upload_dataset(\"Model 1 Telemetry (.csv / .xlsx)\", \"Model 1\", \"upload_m1\")\n        _upload_dataset(\"Model 2 Telemetry (.csv / .xlsx)\", \"Model 2\", \"upload_m2\")\n        _upload_dataset(\"Model 3 Telemetry (.csv / .xlsx)\", \"Model 3\", \"upload_m3\")\n\n        # Auto-load if available in project directory\n        if not st.session_state.model_data:\n            default_path_candidates = {\n                'Model 1': [\n                    r'D:\\acceleration\\Model_1.csv', r'D:\\acceleration\\Model 1.csv',\n                    r'D:\\acceleration\\Model_1.xlsx', r'D:\\acceleration\\Model 1.xlsx',\n                ],\n                'Model 2': [\n                    r'D:\\acceleration\\Model_2.csv', r'D:\\acceleration\\Model 2.csv',\n                    r'D:\\acceleration\\Model_2.xlsx', r'D:\\acceleration\\Model 2.xlsx',\n                ],\n                'Model 3': [\n                    r'D:\\acceleration\\Model_3.csv', r'D:\\acceleration\\Model 3.csv',\n                    r'D:\\acceleration\\Model_3.xlsx', r'D:\\acceleration\\Model 3.xlsx',\n                ],\n            }\n            for model_name, path_list in default_path_candidates.items():\n                if model_name not in st.session_state.model_data:\n                    for p in path_list:\n                        if os.path.exists(p):\n                            df, err = load_dataset(p)\n                            if df is not None:\n                                st.session_state.model_data[model_name] = df\n                                st.session_state.analyses[model_name] = analyze(df)\n                                break\n\n        if st.session_state.model_data:\n            st.caption(f\"Active Models: {', '.join(st.session_state.model_data.keys())}\")\n\n    # Economic Cost Parameters\n    with st.container(border=True):\n        st.markdown(\"**ECONOMIC PARAMETERS**\")\n        scrap_cost = st.slider(\n            \"Scrap Unit Cost ($)\",\n            min_value=5.0, max_value=50.0, value=15.0, step=0.5,\n            format=\"$%.2f\",\n        )\n        downtime_cost = st.slider(\n            \"Downtime Cost ($/min)\",\n            min_value=1.0, max_value=10.0, value=2.50, step=0.25,\n            format=\"$%.2f\",\n        )\n        revenue_mult = st.slider(\n            \"Revenue Multiplier\",\n            min_value=1.5, max_value=8.0, value=4.0, step=0.5,\n            help=\"Unit Selling Price = Scrap Cost x Multiplier\",\n        )\n\n    if st.button(\"Reset Inspection Session\", use_container_width=True):\n        st.session_state.registry.clear()\n        st.session_state.annotated_images.clear()\n        st.success(\"Session reset.\")\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Main Command Header & HUD Telemetry Strip\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nwith st.container(border=True):\n    h_col1, h_col2 = st.columns([3, 1])\n    with h_col1:\n        st.title(\"Autonomous Quality & Process Intelligence\")\n        st.caption(\"YOLOv8 Neural Vision Engine • Theory of Constraints Bottleneck Diagnostics • Predictive Financial Optimization\")\n    with h_col2:\n        st.markdown(\"\"\"\n<div style=\"text-align:right; margin-top:10px;\">\n  <span class=\"badge badge-PASS\"><span class=\"pulse-dot green\"></span>SYSTEM ONLINE</span><br>\n  <small style=\"color:#64748b; font-family:'JetBrains Mono';\">LATENCY: 12ms | LEVEL-4 AI</small>\n</div>\n\"\"\", unsafe_allow_html=True)\n\n    # Live HUD Telemetry Strip\n    st.markdown(\"\"\"\n<div class=\"hud-banner\">\n  <div><span class=\"pulse-dot\"></span>NEURAL INFERENCE: <span class=\"status-val\">GRAD-CAM ACTIVE</span></div>\n  <div>TOC CAPACITY ENGINE: <span class=\"status-val\">MULTI-STAGE ARMORED</span></div>\n  <div>SIMULATION PROTOCOL: <span class=\"status-val\">ARENA v16.2 COMPATIBLE</span></div>\n  <div>ACCURACY CUTOFF: <span class=\"status-val\">DYNAMIC</span></div>\n</div>\n\"\"\", unsafe_allow_html=True)\n\nsummary    = st.session_state.registry.summary()\nanalyses   = st.session_state.analyses\nregistry   = st.session_state.registry\n\n# ── Summary KPI Strip ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nwith st.container(border=True):\n    k1, k2, k3, k4, k5 = st.columns(5)\n    with k1:\n        st.metric(\"Units Inspected\", summary.get('total', 0))\n    with k2:\n        st.metric(\"Defects Identified\", summary.get('defect', 0),\n                  delta=f\"{summary.get('defect_rate', 0):.1f}% defect rate\",\n                  delta_color=\"inverse\")\n    with k3:\n        st.metric(\"Review Required\", f\"{summary.get('uncertain', 0)} / {summary.get('novel', 0)}\")\n    with k4:\n        st.metric(\"Simulation Models\", len(analyses))\n    with k5:\n        st.metric(\"Inference Engine\", \"Active\" if st.session_state.yolo_model else \"Inactive\")\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# TABS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ntab1, tab2, tab3, tab4 = st.tabs([\n    \"Quality Inspection\",\n    \"Production Flow Health\",\n    \"Root Cause Analysis\",\n    \"Profitability & What-If Simulator\",\n])\n\n# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# TAB 1 — QUALITY INSPECTION\n# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nwith tab1:\n    # ── Block 1: Ingestion ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    with st.container(border=True):\n        st.subheader(\"Batch Inspection Ingestion\")\n        st.caption(\"Upload product surface images for automated YOLOv8 classification and neural Grad-CAM localization.\")\n\n        uploaded_files = st.file_uploader(\n            \"Select product surface images\",\n            type=['jpg', 'jpeg', 'png', 'bmp', 'tiff'],\n            accept_multiple_files=True,\n            key=\"img_upload\",\n            label_visibility=\"collapsed\",\n        )\n\n        if uploaded_files:\n            if not st.session_state.yolo_model:\n                st.error(\"YOLOv8 model not loaded. Please verify the model file in the sidebar.\")\n            else:\n                if st.button(\"Run Visual Inspection on Batch\", type=\"primary\", use_container_width=True):\n                    progress_bar = st.progress(0)\n                    for i, f in enumerate(uploaded_files):\n                        img = Image.open(io.BytesIO(f.read())).convert('RGB')\n                        result = run_inference(img, st.session_state.yolo_model, conf_threshold)\n                        st.session_state.registry.add(f.name, result)\n                        st.session_state.annotated_images[f.name] = result\n                        progress_bar.progress((i + 1) / len(uploaded_files))\n\n                    st.success(f\"Batch completed: {len(uploaded_files)} unit(s) evaluated.\")\n\n    # ── Block 2: Gallery Grid ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    reg_df  = registry.to_dataframe()\n    summary = registry.summary()\n\n    if not reg_df.empty and st.session_state.annotated_images:\n        with st.container(border=True):\n            st.subheader(\"Inspection Results Gallery\")\n            st.caption(\"Unit-by-unit classification telemetry, bounding boxes, and Grad-CAM neural evidence overlays.\")\n\n            filter_col1, filter_col2 = st.columns([1, 2])\n            with filter_col1:\n                gal_filter = st.selectbox(\n                    \"Filter Results\",\n                    [\"All Units\", \"Defects Only\", \"Passed Units\", \"Uncertain / Novel\"],\n                    key=\"gal_filter_sel\",\n                )\n            with filter_col2:\n                vis_mode = st.radio(\n                    \"Display Mode\",\n                    [\"Bounding Box\", \"Grad-CAM Heatmap\", \"Clean Industrial View\", \"Raw Image\"],\n                    index=0,\n                    horizontal=True,\n                    key=\"vis_mode_sel\",\n                )\n\n            items = list(st.session_state.annotated_images.items())\n            if gal_filter == \"Defects Only\":\n                items = [it for it in items if it[1]['status'] == 'DEFECT']\n            elif gal_filter == \"Passed Units\":\n                items = [it for it in items if it[1]['status'] == 'PASS']\n            elif gal_filter == \"Uncertain / Novel\":\n                items = [it for it in items if it[1]['status'] in ('UNCERTAIN', 'NOVEL')]\n\n            if not items:\n                st.info(f\"No inspected units match the selected filter: '{gal_filter}'\")\n            else:\n                num_cols = 3\n                for row_idx in range(0, len(items), num_cols):\n                    row_items = items[row_idx:row_idx + num_cols]\n                    cols = st.columns(num_cols)\n                    for col_idx, (fname, res) in enumerate(row_items):\n                        with cols[col_idx]:\n                            with st.container(border=True):\n                                stat = res['status']\n                                dtype = res['defect_type'].upper()\n                                conf = res['confidence'] * 100\n                                bbox = res.get('bbox')\n\n                                top_l, top_r = st.columns([2, 1])\n                                with top_l:\n                                    st.markdown(f\"**{fname}**\")\n                                with top_r:\n                                    st.markdown(f\"<div style='text-align:right;'><span class='badge badge-{stat}'>{stat}</span></div>\", unsafe_allow_html=True)\n\n                                if vis_mode == \"Bounding Box\" and res.get('boxed_image'):\n                                    st.image(res['boxed_image'], use_container_width=True)\n                                elif vis_mode == \"Grad-CAM Heatmap\" and res.get('heatmap_image'):\n                                    st.image(res['heatmap_image'], use_container_width=True)\n                                elif vis_mode == \"Clean Industrial View\" and res.get('annotated_image'):\n                                    st.image(res['annotated_image'], use_container_width=True)\n                                elif vis_mode == \"Raw Image\" and res.get('raw_image'):\n                                    st.image(res['raw_image'], use_container_width=True)\n                                elif res.get('annotated_image'):\n                                    st.image(res['annotated_image'], use_container_width=True)\n\n                                st.markdown(f\"**Class:** `{dtype}` &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Confidence:** `{conf:.1f}%`\")\n                                if bbox:\n                                    x1, y1, x2, y2 = [int(v) for v in bbox]\n                                    st.caption(f\"Target BBox: `[{x1}, {y1}, {x2}, {y2}]` ({x2-x1}x{y2-y1}px)\")\n                                else:\n                                    st.caption(f\"Evaluation: **{stat}** (AI Neural Inference)\")\n\n                                if res.get('class_probs'):\n                                    with st.expander(\"Probability Distribution\"):\n                                        for c_name, c_prob in sorted(res['class_probs'].items(), key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True):\n                                            st.progress(min(1.0, float(c_prob)), text=f\"{c_name.capitalize()}: {c_prob*100:.1f}%\")\n\n        # ── Block 3: Analytics & Log Table ────────────────────────────────────\n        with st.container(border=True):\n            st.subheader(\"Batch Analytics & Telemetry Log\")\n            r1, r2 = st.columns([1, 2])\n            with r1:\n                st.plotly_chart(defect_donut(summary), use_container_width=True, key=\"quality_donut_chart\")\n                if summary.get('by_type'):\n                    st.plotly_chart(defect_type_bar(summary['by_type']), use_container_width=True, key=\"quality_type_bar_chart\")\n\n            with r2:\n                st.markdown(\"##### Detailed Log Table\")\n                styled = reg_df.copy()\n                styled['Status'] = styled['status']\n                st.dataframe(\n                    styled[['unit_id', 'image_name', 'defect_type', 'confidence', 'Status', 'timestamp']],\n                    use_container_width=True, height=270,\n                )\n                if len(reg_df) >= 3:\n                    drift_df = registry.drift_dataframe()\n                    st.plotly_chart(defect_trend(drift_df), use_container_width=True, key=\"quality_defect_trend_chart\")\n\n            if len(reg_df[reg_df['status'] != 'PASS']) > 0:\n                st.plotly_chart(confidence_histogram(reg_df), use_container_width=True, key=\"quality_conf_hist_chart\")\n\n            flagged = flag_novel(reg_df)\n            if not flagged.empty:\n                st.warning(f\"**{len(flagged)} unit(s) flagged for quality review** (UNCERTAIN or NOVEL detections)\")\n                st.dataframe(flagged, use_container_width=True)\n    else:\n        st.info(\"Upload images above and click 'Run Visual Inspection on Batch' to begin analysis.\")\n\n# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# TAB 2 — PRODUCTION FLOW\n# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nwith tab2:\n    if not analyses:\n        st.info(\"Load Model 1/2/3 (.csv or .xlsx) datasets in the sidebar to activate production flow analysis.\")\n    else:\n        # ── Block 1: Production Overview ──────────────────────────────────────\n        with st.container(border=True):\n            st.subheader(\"Production Line Performance & Theory of Constraints\")\n            st.caption(\"Multi-stage capacity utilization, queue times, and Little's Law WIP analysis from Rockwell Arena simulations.\")\n\n            model_names = list(analyses.keys())\n            sel_model   = st.selectbox(\"Select Production Model\", model_names, index=0)\n            analysis    = analyses.get(sel_model)\n\n            if analysis is None:\n                st.error(f\"Unable to parse telemetry for {sel_model}.\")\n            else:\n                m1, m2, m3, m4 = st.columns(4)\n                m1.metric(\"Production Demand\", f\"{analysis['demand']:.0f} units\")\n                m2.metric(\"Parts Produced\",    f\"{analysis['total_parts']:.0f} units\")\n                m3.metric(\"Throughput Rate\",   f\"{analysis['throughput_efficiency']:.1f}%\",\n                          delta=f\"{analysis['throughput_gap']:.0f} units shortage\",\n                          delta_color=\"inverse\")\n                m4.metric(\"Line Speed\",        f\"{analysis['parts_per_hour']:.1f} parts/hr\")\n\n        if analysis is not None:\n            # ── Block 2: Bottleneck Spotlight ─────────────────────────────────\n            with st.container(border=True):\n                st.subheader(\"System Bottleneck Diagnosis\")\n                bn = analysis['bottleneck_station']\n                bu = analysis['bottleneck_util'] * 100\n                bw = analysis['bottleneck_wait']\n\n                if bu > 85:\n                    level = \"CRITICAL\"\n                elif bu > 70:\n                    level = \"WARNING\"\n                else:\n                    level = \"OPTIMAL\"\n\n                st.markdown(f\"\"\"\n<div class=\"evidence-box {'HIGH' if level == 'CRITICAL' else 'MEDIUM' if level == 'WARNING' else 'LOW'}\">\n  <div style=\"display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center;\">\n    <b>Primary Constraint Station: {bn}</b>\n    <span class=\"badge badge-{level}\">{level}</span>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"margin-top:8px;\">\n    <b>Capacity Utilisation:</b> {bu:.1f}% &nbsp;|&nbsp;\n    <b>Average Queue Delay:</b> {bw:.1f} min &nbsp;|&nbsp;\n    <b>Throughput Deficit:</b> {analysis['throughput_gap']:.0f} units\n  </div>\n  <small style=\"color:#94a3b8\">Elevating capacity at this constraint station yields the highest ROI on overall line output.</small>\n</div>\n\"\"\", unsafe_allow_html=True)\n\n            # ── Block 3: Station Telemetry Charts ─────────────────────────────\n            with st.container(border=True):\n                st.subheader(\"Station Capacity & Queue Latency\")\n                ch1, ch2 = st.columns(2)\n                with ch1:\n                    st.plotly_chart(utilization_bar(analysis['stations'], sel_model),\n                                    use_container_width=True, key=f\"flow_util_{sel_model}\")\n                with ch2:\n                    st.plotly_chart(waiting_time_bar(analysis['stations'], sel_model),\n                                    use_container_width=True, key=f\"flow_wait_{sel_model}\")\n\n            # ── Block 4: WIP Estimate ─────────────────────────────────────────\n            wip = estimate_wip(analysis)\n            if any(v > 0 for v in wip.values()):\n                with st.container(border=True):\n                    st.subheader(\"Estimated Work-in-Process (Little's Law)\")\n                    wip_cols = st.columns(len(wip))\n                    for col, (station, count) in zip(wip_cols, wip.items()):\n                        col.metric(f\"{station} WIP Buffer\", f\"~{count:.0f} units\")\n\n            # ── Block 5: Multi-Model Benchmark ────────────────────────────────\n            if len(analyses) > 1:\n                with st.container(border=True):\n                    st.subheader(\"Cross-Model Scenario Benchmark\")\n                    comp_df = compare_models(analyses)\n                    st.dataframe(comp_df, use_container_width=True)\n\n                    if len(analyses) >= 2:\n                        st.plotly_chart(multi_model_radar(analyses), use_container_width=True, key=\"flow_radar_chart\")\n\n# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# TAB 3 — ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS\n# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nwith tab3:\n    no_quality = registry.to_dataframe().empty\n    no_process = not analyses\n\n    if no_quality and no_process:\n        st.info(\"Upload inspection images and production datasets to generate causal links.\")\n    else:\n        # ── Block 1: Causal Correlation ───────────────────────────────────────\n        with st.container(border=True):\n            st.subheader(\"Root-Cause Causal Correlation Engine\")\n            st.caption(\"Evidence-based correlation linking process line overloads with physical defect manifestations.\")\n\n            rc_model = st.selectbox(\n                \"Select Baseline Production Model\",\n                list(analyses.keys()) if analyses else ['No model loaded'],\n                key='rc_model_sel',\n            )\n            rc_analysis  = analyses.get(rc_model) if analyses else None\n            rc_defect_sum = registry.summary()\n\n            evidence = correlate(rc_analysis, rc_defect_sum if not no_quality else None)\n\n            if not evidence:\n                st.success(\"No critical process-quality correlations detected under current operating conditions.\")\n            else:\n                st.markdown(f\"**{len(evidence)} Causal Correlation Rule(s) Triggered**\")\n                for card in evidence:\n                    conf  = card['confidence']\n                    obs   = card['defect_observed']\n                    cls   = conf\n                    html = f\"\"\"\n<div class=\"evidence-box {cls}\">\n  <div style=\"display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; margin-bottom:6px;\">\n    <b>PROBABLE CAUSE: {card['cause']}</b>\n    <span class=\"badge badge-{conf}\">{conf} CONFIDENCE</span>\n  </div>\n  <small><b>Telemetry Evidence:</b> {card['evidence']}</small><br>\n  <small><b>Associated Defect Signatures:</b> {', '.join(card['related_defects']) if card['related_defects'] else 'General throughput bottleneck'}\n  {'&nbsp; <span class=\"badge badge-DEFECT\">OBSERVED IN BATCH</span>' if obs else ''}</small><br>\n  <hr style=\"margin:8px 0; border-color:#24324c\">\n  <small><b>Recommended Corrective Action:</b> {card['action']}</small>\n</div>\n\"\"\"\n                    st.markdown(html, unsafe_allow_html=True)\n\n        # ── Block 2: Drift Monitoring ─────────────────────────────────────────\n        with st.container(border=True):\n            st.subheader(\"Batch-to-Batch Defect Drift\")\n            if no_quality or len(registry) < 2:\n                st.info(\"Inspect at least 2 units in Tab 1 to track process drift.\")\n            else:\n                drift_df_raw = registry.drift_dataframe()\n                drift        = drift_analysis(drift_df_raw)\n\n                if drift:\n                    dc1, dc2, dc3 = st.columns(3)\n                    dc1.metric(\"Drift Trajectory\", drift['trend'])\n                    dc2.metric(\"Drift Rate\", f\"{drift['slope']:+.2f} pp/unit\")\n                    dc3.metric(\"Flagged Review Units\", drift['novel_count'] + drift['uncertain_count'])\n\n                    st.plotly_chart(defect_trend(drift['df']), use_container_width=True, key=\"rootcause_defect_trend_chart\")\n\n        # ── Block 3: Out-of-Distribution Registry ─────────────────────────────\n        if not no_quality:\n            flagged = flag_novel(registry.to_dataframe())\n            if not flagged.empty:\n                with st.container(border=True):\n                    st.subheader(\"Out-of-Distribution & Human Review Registry\")\n                    st.warning(f\"**{len(flagged)} Novel / Uncertain Unit(s)** — Flagged for manual engineering review.\")\n                    st.dataframe(flagged, use_container_width=True)\n\n# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# TAB 4 — PROFITABILITY & RECOMMENDATIONS\n# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nwith tab4:\n    if not analyses:\n        st.info(\"Upload production CSV or Excel datasets in the sidebar to activate the financial engine.\")\n    else:\n        # ── Block 1: Baseline Economics ───────────────────────────────────────\n        with st.container(border=True):\n            st.subheader(\"Baseline Economic Impact & Loss Waterfall\")\n            st.caption(\"Financial translation of scrap losses, bottleneck idle time, and opportunity costs.\")\n\n            fin_model = st.selectbox(\n                \"Select Financial Model Target\",\n                list(analyses.keys()),\n                key='fin_model_sel',\n            )\n            fin_analysis  = analyses.get(fin_model)\n            fin_defect_sum = registry.summary() if not registry.to_dataframe().empty else None\n\n            if fin_analysis is None:\n                st.error(\"Unable to load financial model data.\")\n            else:\n                baseline = compute_financials(\n                    fin_analysis, fin_defect_sum, scrap_cost, downtime_cost, revenue_mult\n                )\n\n                fb1, fb2, fb3, fb4, fb5 = st.columns(5)\n                fb1.metric(\"Gross Revenue\",    f\"${baseline['gross_revenue']:,.0f}\")\n                fb2.metric(\"Scrap Loss\",       f\"${baseline['scrap_loss']:,.0f}\", delta_color=\"inverse\")\n                fb3.metric(\"Idle Cost\",        f\"${baseline['bottleneck_idle_loss']:,.0f}\", delta_color=\"inverse\")\n                fb4.metric(\"Opportunity Loss\", f\"${baseline['opportunity_loss']:,.0f}\", delta_color=\"inverse\")\n                fb5.metric(\"Operating Margin\",\n                           f\"${baseline['net_margin']:,.0f}\",\n                           delta=f\"{baseline['margin_pct']:.1f}%\",\n                           delta_color=\"normal\" if baseline['net_margin'] > 0 else \"inverse\")\n\n                wf1, wf2 = st.columns([3, 2])\n                with wf1:\n                    st.plotly_chart(financial_waterfall(baseline, fin_model), use_container_width=True, key=f\"fin_waterfall_{fin_model}\")\n\n                with wf2:\n                    st.markdown(\"##### Direct Loss Breakdown\")\n                    loss_items = {\n                        \"Scrap Material Losses\": baseline['scrap_loss'],\n                        \"Bottleneck Idle Overhead\": baseline['bottleneck_idle_loss'],\n                        \"Market Opportunity Deficit\": baseline['opportunity_loss'],\n                        \"Estimated Rework Cost\": baseline['rework_cost'],\n                    }\n                    for label, val in loss_items.items():\n                        pct = val / baseline['total_loss'] * 10